{"sid": "172bfa38-8de4-42ee-a6dd-29574ca856a8", "uid": "9d766f1f-50c6-4668-bb17-eabebe25e8a7", "seq": 2, "ts": 1791458603.97982, "plan_id": null, "event": {"type": "user_message", "kind": "message", "content": "I tested the partner programme end to end and found these issues. Please fix all of them in this project, then verify that every changed object deploys and runs cleanly:\n\n1. Approving a partner failed with \"column partner_id of relation surz_discount does not exist\". SURZ_DISCOUNT's new columns (PARTNER_ID, PARTNER_NAME, USAGE_COUNT) were never deployed. Deploy every object whose model or Database_Design you changed, including surz_discount, and backfill USAGE_COUNT = 0 where it is NULL (TENDER10 has NULL).\n2. WELCOME_SENT_ON is stamped on approve even though the email was only queued, and the IOFlow delivery then failed (\"IOFlow connection not configured\"). Do not claim the email was sent. Either rename the field to \"Welcome queued on\" or stamp it only when delivery is confirmed.\n3. APPROVED_BY, ADD_USER and CHG_USER are blank on the partner and on the discount row created by Approve. Stamp them with the acting user.\n4. portal_url in the approval event payload is \"/surz_partner_order\". It must point to the partner portal page (/partner-portal).\n5. The Approve and Reject buttons show on an already APPROVED or REJECTED partner when the record is open. visible_when only hides them in the list menu, so the server-side refusal is the only guard. Hide or disable them on the open record too.\n6. The self-registration form must not show the Approve/Reject buttons or the admin-only fields (discount code, discount %, reject reason, approved by, welcome sent on). A blank registration form must not open with a pending unsaved change (\"Save (1)\"). The \"Apply now\" link must work inside the Run view.\n7. ORDER DISCOUNT CODE: there must be NO lookup or picker on the discount code. The customer knows the code from the influencer channel and types it in. Make it a plain text entry. On entry, validate it server-side (must be an active code, case-insensitive). Fill the discount % and partner straight away through item_change, so the percent shows before saving. If the code is unknown, show a clear error. The order lines grid must show the per-line discount without a reload after save.\n8. Partner portal (\"My partner account\" / \"My referred orders\"): remove the \"+ Add\" button from read-only lists, hide admin columns, and format timestamps as dates. On the admin Partners list, put Status near the front so pending applications are visible. Make the QR field read-only (no \"Add image\").\n9. PARTNERS ARE PROJECT USERS: a partner signs up through the application's own self-registration (\"Create an account\" on the Run sign-in). Self-registered users get the default role (currently \"customer\"). Make sure a self-registered project user can open \"Become a partner\", submit an application, and after approval see ONLY their own partner record and their own referred orders, never another partner's. Use row security keyed on the registry user id. Admin screens (Partners approval, Discount codes, Partner sales dashboard) must not be visible to a self-registered user. If a separate \"partner\" role is needed after approval, grant it from the Approve action, or tell me which way you chose.", "client_id": "5356fa01-affb-4e38-87d1-94b1416a0a5d", "device": null, "seq": 2}}
